    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What is the smallest component Hana can place on an SMT line?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Hana places 01005 passives and supports micro-BGA and WLCSP attachment to 0.2 mm pitch, with QFP packages to 0.4 mm pitch.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Does Hana inspect every board, or only high-reliability work?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Solder-paste inspection, 3D AOI and X-ray are part of the standard SMT process, with full material, unit and product traceability. These controls are not limited to automotive or medical programs.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can an SMT program transfer between Hana sites?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. SMT is qualified across China, Thailand, Cambodia and the USA, allowing programs to move between sites through documented first-article qualification rather than a complete re-NPI.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What board and panel sizes can Hana handle?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">PCB panels up to 440 × 600 mm are supported, with convection reflow in air or nitrogen and vacuum nitrogen reflow available.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What quality and certification systems cover SMT?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Customer IP is protected under ISO 27001. Hana also operates dedicated medical and automotive assembly lines within fully ESD-controlled facilities.</div>
    </details>
